module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unrun_self_witnessed_module_reads_as_coverage

import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }
import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }

data unrun_self_witnessed_module_reads_as_coverage: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unrun_self_witnessed_module_reads_as_coverage" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "CLASS: a module in a `witness_layer_roots` layer declares `test fn` bodies whose only audience is its own file, and the file sits outside `gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots` `witness_discovery_scan_dirs`. CI never discovers it, so the assertions never execute -- yet the test syntax reads as coverage to every reader after it, including the reader who wrote it. This is rung honesty (DESIGN section 4b) applied to a whole file rather than one name: a type name, a diagnostic variant, an inert lens or a plan establishes nothing, and neither does an unrun `test fn`.",
    "INVALID STATE: a file passes the compiler, contains test bodies that would fail if the code they describe regressed, and contributes zero refusal to CI. The mutation the tests exist to catch can be introduced and the floor stays green. The state is invisible precisely because the file looks like a witness: `test fn` is a rung marker, and nothing distinguishes a discovered one from an undiscovered one at the site where it is read.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: rung 0 -- syntactic. At 0dc3f0ab4c1fe112c13b10d6cbc991a94f3744fd, `src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag` carried `orch_while_path_kind_discriminates_regular_directory_missing_holds`, which pins one bracket operator per `std.filesystem.types` `EntryKind`. Deleting its only production route through that lowering (the located-assign chain in `test.extdeps.languages.bash_orch_if`) turned NOTHING red anywhere: the same assertion existed in exactly one other file, and that one is in the population below. The mutation survives, the compiles stay at `0 blocking error(s)`, and the witness count in the prose does not move. Found while deciding whether a deletion was safe -- which is the moment this class costs something.",
    "POPULATION AND ITS QUERY, measured 2026-10-19 at origin/main 45fdd502248972781b5f6358321f1e46f090343c -- not transcribed counts. Both lists are read live from `dag/gunbc/ci/ci_layer_roots.dag` (`witness_layer_roots` = [\"dag\", \"src/v2\"]; `witness_discovery_scan_dirs` = [\"dag/test/claim\", \"src/v2/test/claim/manual\", \"src/v2/test/claim/emit\"]), so the query re-derives itself against the authority rather than against this receipt. Re-derive at the head you are standing on: `python3 - <<'PY' import re,glob,os LAYER=[\"dag\",\"src/v2\"] SCAN=[\"dag/test/claim\",\"src/v2/test/claim/manual\",\"src/v2/test/claim/emit\"] rows=[] for root in LAYER: for p in glob.glob(root+\"/**/*.dag\",recursive=True): tf=len(re.findall(r'^test fn ',open(p).read(),re.M)) if tf==0: continue rel=os.path.relpath(p,'.') if any(rel==d or rel.startswith(d+'/') for d in SCAN): continue if '/test/' in '/'+rel: continue rows.append((rel,tf)) print(sorted(rows,key=lambda r:-r[1]),sum(n for _,n in rows)) PY` -> 7 self-witnessed PRODUCTION modules, 67 test bodies: `src/v2/workflow/orchestration_retry_emit.dag` 17, `src/v2/workflow/orchestration_emit.dag` 16, `src/v2/workflow/orchestration_bash.dag` 12, `src/v2/lens/mandatory_tag/corpus_scan_witness.dag` 8, `src/v2/workflow/orchestration_tier2_emit.dag` 8, `src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag` 4, `src/v2/lens/no_dual_representation.dag` 2. None of the seven is named in `dag/gunbc/ci/ci_layer_roots.dag` (grep per basename: 0 hits), so no discovered CI layer runs any of them. Per-function enrolment was measured as well, since a module can be unrostered while individual functions are named elsewhere: 63 of the 67 appear by name nowhere outside their own file. The 4 exceptions are all in `src/v2/lens/mandatory_tag/corpus_scan_witness.dag` (`corpus_live_clean_tree_wall_holds`, `corpus_projection_missing_plant_reads_absent`, `corpus_projection_file_plant_reads_non_external_scheme`, `corpus_projection_real_anchor_reads_https`), named as `ClaimRun` entries in `gunbc.instruments.extdeps_external_authority_transport` -- whose only discovered consumer, `test.claim.cheap_gate_pool`, asserts the pool's CHUNKING (`claims_covered_by_cheap_pool_chunks`) and does not execute the entries. `gunbc.declined_live_tree_defect_classification` also names two of them and says of itself that it \"is not an expected-red enrolment and must never become one\", so it is a decline record rather than a lane. Net: 0 of the 67 are executed by any path in CI.",
    "THE COUNTING DISCIPLINE THIS ROW OWES, stated because the naive figure is wrong and was almost used: widening the query to every non-scan-dir file with a `test fn` -- including the `src/v2/test/**` tree, whose entries are run by name from explicit registries -- returns 886 files and 6310 test bodies. That number measures the gap between one discovery mechanism and the whole corpus, not an unrun population, and calling it the population would be this row's own failure mode committed inside the row about it. A cost row is NOT an execution claim and must not be read as one: 42 of the 59 `test.workflow.orchestration_*` bodies have rows in `gunbc.witness.witness_row_cost_basis.tsv` with `eval_ms_basis`, which looks like a receipt for having been run. All 1146 rows in that file -- the whole corpus, not just these -- carry the SAME `run_ref` 30550328673 and host_class `srv_fleet_arm64`, i.e. one seeding batch from which the basis figures were read, and the file's own header says a row is established by \"first fleet observation\". So it evidences that someone ran them once, outside CI, and evidences nothing about whether any path runs them today. Claiming `never executes anywhere ever` would be unfalsifiable prose; claiming `no path in CI discovers or runs them` is decidable, and that is what this row claims. What is claimed, and is all the mechanism supports, is that NO PATH IN CI DISCOVERS OR RUNS THEM. A dated receipt is not an execution guarantee either way -- which is the softer half of the same defect.",
    "HARM: the assertions can regress silently and every downstream reader is misled twice -- once by the file's own `test fn` markers, and again by any prose that cites the module as the reason a behavior is covered. The `While` emit arm (`compiler.emit_orchestration` `orch_emit_while_step`) is the live example: its only falsifier was an undiscovered self-test, so a malformed While lowering ships green, while `docs/plans/shell-to-dag-residual-census-and-arc-completion.md` and `gunbc.plans.shell_emission_model` each described While emit as covered.",
    "CEILING: STRUCTURAL, NOT DECIDABLE FROM THE NODE TREE, AND THIS IS THE DEFICIT. `test fn` carries no discovered-ness fact, and discovery is a directory predicate read at run time by `src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs` (`witness_discovery_scan_dirs()`), so a module in a `witness_layer_roots` layer compiles identically whether or not anyone will ever execute its tests. The compiler cannot refuse it because the fact is not in the declaration. A rung-3 alternative exists and was NOT taken here because it is a CI-policy change, wider than a ledger row: a coherence witness that refuses when a module in a layer root declares `test fn` bodies, lies outside every scan dir, and is named by no execution roster -- turning the population into a refusal instead of a fact. `gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots` already registers namespaces that are deliberately non-executing (`non_executing_witness_module_prefixes` = [\"v1\"]), so the distinction between 'deliberately unrun' and 'unrun by accident' is expressible in the authority and simply is not enforced for the layer roots.",
    "TRIGGER -- what dissolves this row: an operator CI-policy decision. Either (a) add `src/v2/workflow` (and the two `src/v2/lens` files) to `witness_discovery_scan_dirs`, which makes the 67 assertions execute but also pulls in the whole self-witnessed family and its cost, or (b) delete the population along with the code it guards, or (c) install the coherence witness above so an unrun self-witness refuses at compile time. The decision is outward-facing (it changes what CI executes and pays for) and belongs to the operator, not to whoever notices. Until then the population is measured by the query above and re-measured by anyone who reads it.",
    "MEASUREMENT NOTE, so this row does not itself become stale prose: the population is a function of two lists in `gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots` plus the tree, so it is re-derived, never copied. If scan dirs widen, the population shrinks automatically and the receipts above are a dated observation about 0dc3f0ab -- which is exactly how a dated capture should read.",
    "ISLAND NAMED AS THE DELETION TRIGGER'S POPULATION -- PROPOSED, NOT BUILT, AND HEADED AS MEASURED. Scope, in the order the consumers fall away: `src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag` has 0 importers, 4 unrun self-tests, and is the only constructor of `PipelineStep::While` outside `src/v2/test/claim/effect_plan_bash_materialize.dag` -- true at origin/main 45fdd5022489 and unchanged by any PR in flight. Behind it sits the spelling chain `test.extdeps.languages.bash_orch_if` `bash_dirname_ascent_target_model` -> `v2.extdeps.languages.bash_orch_tier2` `orch_cmdsubst_assign_call_target_model` -> `orch_call_target_model` -> `bash_orch_call_target_model`. MEASURED HEADS DISAGREE ABOUT WHO ELSE HOLDS THE DOOR, so each is stated: at origin/main 45fdd5022489 `bash_dirname_ascent_target_model` has TWO callers, `orchestration_while_emit.dag:141` and `bash_orch_if`'s own `bash_nearest_ancestor_locate_body_command`; at the head of the carve PR #14489 the second is deleted, leaving `orchestration_while_emit.dag:141` as the only caller outside the definition, and only then is the chain reachable from nowhere but an undiscovered self-test. smart-heron-455's ladder cut removes the `realize_call:` binding in `v2.extdeps.languages.bash_orchestration_emit`, which is the other way in. The `PathPredicate` lowering `bash_path_predicate_target_model` is entered externally only by `orchestration_while_emit` plus the witness ported in #14489. Deleting the whole unit also strands `std.path_intent` `DirnameAscent`, `PathPredicate`/`PathEntryKind`/`PathNotEq`, and `extdeps.linux.proc_self_cgroup` `proc_self_cgroup_absolute_path_from_relative` -- the last has a consumer at main (`src/v2/extdeps/languages/bash_proc_self_cgroup.dag:43`) and so is LISTED, not deleted, until #14467 removes that file. RECOMMENDATION: do NOT delete in one PR while the trigger above is undecided. If scan-dir enrolment is chosen, those 67 assertions become the cheapest real coverage in the tree and the island is worth keeping; deleting first and enrolling second throws away tests that would have worked. The query in the POPULATION receipt, not this paragraph, is the authority on what is in the population -- re-run it at the head you stand on, because the two PRs in flight move which callers exist."
  ],
  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "witness_discovery_scan_dirs"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "witness_layer_roots"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "non_executing_witness_module_prefixes"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.orchestration_while_emit", decl_name: "orch_while_path_kind_discriminates_regular_directory_missing_holds"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.workflow.orchestration_retry_emit", decl_name: "orch_retry_byte_identical_to_hand_authored_holds"),
  ],
}
